  "scope": "Windows/Linux each pass twenty native suites, ten background repetitions, four background GL contexts, one installed public C++ command/job consumer and 3310 installed Python checks, zero failure/error/skip. Fifty-four new Python cases cover captured intent, full original-record validation before strict replay/rebinding, lossless numeric rules, stale source domains, masks/positioned ROIs, metadata-only admission, publication failure atomicity and escaped-preview reservation lifetime. Twelve new actual ImageJ 1.54r Apply/reset cases cover UInt8/UInt16 whole/partial/constant data, configured and observed display ranges, threshold clearing and palette preservation. All 64 prior full-domain arithmetic vectors and prior 3256 selected regressions pass. Native fixtures additionally cover blocked worker-only virtual reads, queued source release, cooperative running/ready cancellation, shutdown, publication guards, plane-alias leases and reentrant caller changes to frozen inputs. Final qualification fingerprints actual compiled source trees against a fresh Windows manifest; Linux Python runs use a byte-verified native filesystem snapshot of 5467 test/config/fixture files. Both final installed origins and retained product bytes are checked. All 1297 input registrations, original 99 requirement/status triples and the commercial-use dependency inventory are preserved. This is scoped command/job/reset qualification, not an ImGui Apply route or complete G057/platform/resource acceptance.",
