  "remaining": [
    "Captured commands, strict/rebind APIs and worker preparation/publication are available through C++/Python. Connect them to the Window host: active owner and busy policy, wait/cancel/close, staged workflow recording, diagnostics and shared OperationTargetPanel T/C/Z/ROI controls. The contrast panel still has no Apply button.",
    "Add editor record-schema dispatch, explicit rebind review and native workflow/batch-language integration; the standalone native replay/rebind APIs are not yet editor workflow support.",
    "RGB Apply requires independent color-controller reference behavior before enabling it; RGBA is a separate extension. Floating Apply remains unavailable consistently with ImageJ scalar support.",
    "Processor reset now clears threshold, preserves palettes and uses observed UInt16 or configured full display bounds. Broader multi-channel representative-plane, empty-target, custom default-range, signed/intensity calibration and UI reference acceptance remain open. Empty masks retain the explicit native no-change/no-IO extension.",
    "Exact upstream slider normalization, log histogram/control/calibration and Set/Reset traces remain unqualified. Float64, IEEE-preserving Float32 and packed RGB/RGBA histogram/Auto are not enabled in the current panel.",
    "Finite legacy automatic range scans and other analysis/editing paths can still acquire pixels synchronously. Source caches, allocator/frontend and publication/history allocations are outside declared job reservations; full responsiveness/resource/platform acceptance remains open."
